Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear all,
I downloaded from the Phyloiwiki the code for BSM for time-stratified analysis.
By default, the script is set to 50 BSMs.
But I want to perform 1000 BSMs. When I changed 50 to 1000, the code stopped in that point and did not run.
How do I do?
Thanks

From u115d05260b0c341a at groups.google.com  Sat Sep  3 00:29:31 2022
From: u115d05260b0c341a at groups.google.com (Nick Matzke)
Date: Sat, 03 Sep 2022 00:29:31 +0000
Subject: Re: [BioGeoBEARS] BSM - how to change number of iterations
Message-ID: <PDooXhKbsK8.emfTk2IdBgAJ@biogeobears.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <PDooXhKbsK8.ivd4mwbzBQAJ@biogeobears.groups.google.com>
References: <PDooXhKbsK8.ivd4mwbzBQAJ@biogeobears.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/biogeobears/c/PDooXhKbsK8/m/emfTk2IdBgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I think you need to change this:

maxnum_maps_to_try=100, nummaps_goal=50, maxtries_per_branch=40000

...to e.g. this:

maxnum_maps_to_try=2000, nummaps_goal=1000, maxtries_per_branch=40000

That said, 100 stochastic maps is probably 99% as good as 1000.

Cheers,
Nick

